1`, category 1 ↔ `y=0`); on a 3-category family the category probabilities sum to 1, the score is zero-mean (`Σ_k P(k)·score(k)=0`), the score matches a central finite difference of the loglik (rtol 1e-5), the observed weight matches `−(second finite difference)` and is strictly `> 0` (rtol 1e-3); an END-TO-END value gate confirms the ordinal Laplace marginal at `θ=[0]` equals the Bernoulli-probit marginal on the same binary data recoded `1/2` (`laplace_marginal_loglik`, Δ ~1e-16); and strictly-increasing / non-empty threshold plus `1:K` category-range guards throw. A ≥3-category ordinal design is MORE informative than a binary threshold (cf. `V6-PROBIT`), which is the point of the motivating calving-ease trait (T1). JOINT ESTIMATION (doc-20 Step 1): `fit_laplace_reml(...; family = :ordered_probit)` now estimates σ²a AND the `K-1` cutpoints jointly by an IDENTIFIED reparameterization — fix `θ_1 = 0` and estimate `θ_2..θ_{K-1}` via positive increments `θ_j = θ_{j-1} + exp(δ_j)` (strict ordering automatic), K read from the data; the outer NelderMead objective is guarded (a σ²a safety-rail `|log σ²a − log σ²a₀| ≤ 8` + a singular/non-finite penalty) so the weakly-identified small-data MLE cannot run to the boundary. Validated (`test/runtests.jl`, T1 fit): the K=2 fit reduces EXACTLY to `fit_laplace_reml(...; family = :bernoulli_probit)` (σ²a rtol 1e-3, marginal loglik atol 1e-5, `cutpoints == [0]`); the K=3 fit on a structured pedigree returns strictly-ordered cutpoints (`θ_1=0 < θ_2`), a rail-bounded σ²a, a self-consistent marginal loglik at the estimate, and `converged`; guards reject `< 1`/non-integer codes and `marginal = :variational`. SAME-ESTIMAND COMPARATOR RUN (2026-07-01): `ordinal::clmm` (Laplace-ML, probit — glmmTMB does NOT fit cumulative-link ordinal) on an identical A=I / repeated-records K=3 packet (80 animals × 4 records) agrees with the `:ordered_probit` joint fit — cutpoint SPACING Δ 0.004 (essentially exact, after aligning the intercept convention), σ²a Δ 0.024 (ML-vs-REML), intercept Δ 0.012, both converged (`docs/dev-log/recovery-checkpoints/2026-07-01-ordinal-clmm-comparator.md`). PRE-DECLARED 48-SEED RECOVERY GATE PASSED (2026-07-01): known-truth A=I/repeated-records K=3 recovery on an INFORMATIVE design (`sim/phase6_ordinal_recovery.jl`, predeclared `3bef5b03` before the run) — 48/48 converged, `|bias| ≤ 2·MCSE` for σ²a (bias +0.027, 1.44·MCSE — the weak axis), the cutpoint θ_2 (0.58·MCSE), AND β; no detectable bias (`docs/dev-log/recovery-checkpoints/2026-07-01-ordinal-recovery-48seed.md`); the informative design resolves the small-data weak-identification.",
