-        "COVERED (SCOPED, validation-scale, opt-in; NOT the public default — public-covered FITTING stays 1 = v0.1 Gaussian) via the doc-16 G11 substitutable gate, path (b): one same-estimand comparator leg (`glmmTMB Gamma(link=\"log\")`) plus a passing pre-declared 48-seed recovery gate. \"Covered\" means the engine correctly implements Gamma-log JOINT estimation of σ²a + the shape ν on an informative A=I/repeated-records design — NOT small-sample accuracy (bias within 2·MCSE for σ²a and ν; read as no detectable bias, never \"unbiased\"). SCOPE OF VALIDITY: A=I/repeated-records single design (q=80×4=320 obs), Laplace-only, dense, asymptotic, INTERNAL. STANDING DEBT (covered does NOT retire it): broader-DGP + pedigree-A (non-I) recovery; a 2nd same-estimand comparator (MCMCglmm has NO general Gamma family — glmmTMB is the same-estimand tool; a 2nd REML leg is owed); the `:symbol` payload + scale-labelled observation-scale h² (the NS-2017 trigamma observation form); and R activation. `GammaResponse(shape)` (internal) extends the non-Gaussian engine to a STRICTLY-POSITIVE CONTINUOUS response with the log link: mean `μ = exp(η)`, SUPPLIED shape `ν > 0`, `y | η ~ Gamma(shape ν, mean μ)` with density `(ν/μ)^ν y^{ν-1} e^{-νy/μ}/Γ(ν)`. The conditional `ℓ = ν(log ν − η) + (ν−1)log y − ν y e^{-η} − log Γ(ν)` is LOG-CONCAVE in η, so the score `ν(y e^{-η} − 1)` and the OBSERVED-information IRLS weight `ν y e^{-η}` are exact and strictly `> 0` — the SAME convention as Poisson/probit (no Fisher-scoring substitution, in contrast to the beta-binomial). Reuses the module's existing `_loggamma` (no new dependency). Validated (`test/runtests.jl`, T-Gamma): the `ν = 1` REDUCTION to the EXPONENTIAL is EXACT for loglik/score/observed weight (`ℓ = −η − y e^{-η}`); on a `ν ∈ {0.5, 2, 5}` × `(y, η)` grid the score matches a central finite difference of the loglik (rtol 1e-5) and the observed weight matches `−(second finite difference)` and is `> 0` (rtol 1e-3); the Laplace marginal is finite end-to-end on a Gamma fixture; and positive-shape / strictly-positive-response guards throw. JOINT ESTIMATION: `fit_laplace_reml(...; family = :gamma)` now estimates σ²a AND the shape ν jointly over `(log σ²a, log ν)` by NelderMead (the same shape as `:nbinom`; `theta_init` seeds ν), with a SAFETY RAIL bounding `log σ²a` and `log ν` to init ± 8 (uninformative data — few subjects / no replication — weakly identifies ν through a flat large-ν likelihood, so the raw optimum can run away; the rail prevents it, matching the ordinal σ²a guard). Validated (`test/runtests.jl`, T-Gamma fit): on an INFORMATIVE A=I / repeated-records fixture (q=6 subjects × 4 replicate records; replication identifies ν) the fit converges with a meaningfully positive σ²a (`> 1e-3`) and a BOUNDED shape (`0 < ν < 1e4`), a self-consistent marginal loglik at the estimate, and beats a deliberately off-optimum `(σ²a, ν)`; strictly-positive-response + `:variational` guards throw. SAME-ESTIMAND COMPARATOR RUN (2026-07-01): `glmmTMB` `Gamma(link=\"log\")` + `(1|id)` on an identical A=I / repeated-records packet agrees with `fit_laplace_reml(...; family=:gamma)` — shape ν Δ 0.003 (essentially exact), σ²a Δ 0.017 / intercept Δ 0.032 (the expected ML-vs-REML variance gap), both converged (`docs/dev-log/recovery-checkpoints/2026-07-01-gamma-glmmtmb-comparator.md`). PRE-DECLARED 48-SEED RECOVERY GATE PASSED (2026-07-01): known-truth A=I / repeated-records recovery (`sim/phase6_gamma_recovery.jl`, predeclared BEFORE the run) — 48/48 converged, `|bias| ≤ 2·MCSE` for σ²a AND ν, re-confirmed byte-identical post-rail (commit `7666b656`); read as no detectable bias, never \"unbiased\" (`docs/dev-log/recovery-checkpoints/2026-07-01-gamma-recovery-48seed.md`).",
